          "content": {
            "id": "b9a0c054-893c-3bdc-a044-4a762ea0673d",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Banks kick off earnings, Fed Chair Powell speaks: What to Watch",
            "description": "<p>Market Domination Overtime host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a> takes a look at the top stories for investors to watch on Tuesday, Oct. 14.</p>\n<p>Earnings season kicks off, with JPMorgan Chase (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JPM\">JPM</a>), Wells Fargo (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/WFC\">WFC</a>), Goldman Sachs (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GS\">GS</a>), Citi (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/C\">C</a>), BlackRock (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BLK\">BLK</a>), and Johnson & Johnson (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JNJ\">JNJ</a>) all reporting results.</p>\n<p>Federal Reserve commentary is expected from Fed Chair Jerome Powell, Fed Vice Chair for Supervision Michelle Bowman, Fed Governor Christopher Waller, and Boston Fed President Susan Collins.</p>\n<p>The Small Business Association's (SBA's) National Federation of Independent Business (NFIB) September Small Business Optimism Index will be published in the morning. Economists are expecting a slight decrease from the prior month.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:8;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination-overtime/\">Market Domination Overtime</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "Market Domination Overtime host Josh Lipton takes a look at the top stories for investors to watch on Tuesday, Oct. 14. Earnings season kicks off, with JPMorgan Chase (JPM), Wells Fargo (WFC), Goldman Sachs (GS), Citi (C), BlackRock (BLK), and Johnson & Johnson (JNJ) all reporting results. Federal Reserve commentary is expected from Fed Chair Jerome Powell, Fed Vice Chair for Supervision Michelle Bowman, Fed Governor Christopher Waller, and Boston Fed President Susan Collins. The Small Business Association's (SBA's) National Federation of Independent Business (NFIB) September Small Business Optimism Index will be published in the morning. Economists are expecting a slight decrease from the prior month. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more Market Domination Overtime.",
