            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Big Bank earnings: What to watch from JPMorgan, Citi, & more",
            "description": "<p>Big Bank earnings (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/XLF\">XLF</a>) are kicking off next week, with Goldman Sachs (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/GS\">GS</a>), JPMorgan Chase (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JPM\">JPM</a>), Wells Fargo (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/WFC\">WFC</a>), and Citi (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/C\">C</a>) reporting on Tuesday, Oct. 14. Bank of America (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/BAC\">BAC</a>) will report on Wednesday, Oct. 15.</p>\n<p>Whalen Global Advisors chairman, Chris Whalen, sits down with Market Catalysts host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/julie-hyman/\">Julie Hyman</a> to discuss what he will be watching for as Big Bank earnings roll out.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:8;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
